* The scattering plane is formed by placing the incoming \(e^{+}e^{-}\) pair in the same plane as one outgoing hadron, where the outgoing hadron momentum defines the \(\hat{n}\)-axis (Figure 1.9a). In this case, the angle \(\phi_{0}\) is the angle between the scattering plane and other outgoing hadron momentum, measured around \(\hat{n}\). Then, the extracted asymmetry, \(A_{0}\), is the coefficient of the \(\cos(2\phi_{0})\) term in the cross section.
