The best case scenario for a calibration of the BEMC would have numerous light, charged particles whose mass may be safely ignored at high energies, such as electrons, detected in each tower. The momentum will be known well from the TPC, so the ratio of energy to momentum (E/p) can be calculated by measuring the energy deposited

