The other axis of the histogram holds the kinematic information about jet \(p_{T}\), \(z\), and \(j_{T}\). Tables 5.2 - 5.4 outline the kinematic bins used for the analysis. These bins were chosen to optimize the sampled physics while also ensuring the statistical power of each bin is good enough to calculate asymmetries. When the two-dimensional histograms are filled, the angle is known and the kinematic value is known, so there is a bin waiting for that value. These yields now hold all of the transverse spin asymmetry modulations, and they must now be extracted.

